<title>MEXICO: ICA may take stake in Argentine firm.</title>
<headline>ICA may take stake in Argentine firm.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican construction giant Empresas ICA said on Thursday it had signed a memorandum of understanding for an option to acquire 50 percent of Argentine construction firm Comercial del Plata Construcciones (CPC).</p>
<p>Terms were not announced, but construction analysts have estimated half of CPC's value at $30 million.</p>
<p>&quot;The objective of this possible association is to position ICA in the Mercosur markets,&quot; ICA said in a statement, referring to the South American trading bloc.</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez, Monterrey bureau, +528 345-7617))</p>
